# 0304 = 0303 plus independent config-order / queue-lifecycle / doorbell
# axes.  Defaults reproduce the 0303 behaviour.
#   ruby_cfg_pre=0|1       configure EP2 before SET_CONFIGURATION status ACK
#   ruby_qstart_cfg=0|1    Q_START the empty TX ring at config
#   ruby_qstart_keep=0|1   keep started across drain (RESUME per enqueue)
#   ruby_txbell=0|1        1 ms Q_START doorbell when FIFO has data
#   ruby_txbell_ms=1..100  doorbell interval (0 ms disproved)
#   ruby_tx_eprst_bit=<n>  EP_RST bit override; default 1<<(16+txep)
# Arms: D 0/0/0/0; A1 cfg_pre=1; A2 qstart_cfg=1; A3 qstart_keep=1;
# B1 txbell=1; C1 cfg_pre+qstart_cfg+qstart_keep; C2 all four.
# Primary endpoint is EP1; EP3 is only an EP_RST sanity arm.
# Boot cmdline base: 0303 minus `ruby_txep=3 ruby_txfbase=128` and the
# touch-only `sweetgt`/`sweetgtspispeed` pair; 544 B <= 607.
# ---
# 0303 = 0302 plus the TX endpoint/FIFO parameterisation (one build,
# zero-build arms). Vendor profile only; ACM forces EP1/0.
#   ruby_txep=1|3        echo TX endpoint (1 = EP1 0x81, 3 = EP3 0x83)
#   ruby_txfbase=<dec>   TXnCSR2 FIFO address field (dec 128 = 0x80)
# Arms: A default 1/0; B 3/128 (vendor adb EP3); C 1/128; D 3/0.
# First test image cmdline: ruby_txep=3 ruby_txfbase=128.
# ---
# 0302 = 0301 plus the echo/descriptor decoupling:
#   ruby_echo=1 makes the vendor profile (ruby_enum=0) use the same echo
#   data plane and TX QMU configuration as ACM; descriptors stay vendor.
#   Default: ruby_acm_cmd (profile 1/2 echo, profile 0 no echo).
# ---
# 0301 = 0300 plus zero-build enumeration/ZLP axes:
#   ruby_enum=0|1|2  0 vendor 0xFF (WinUSB), 1 CDC-ACM (COM), 2 ACM with
#                    device class 0xEF/0x02/0x01 (explicit composite).
#                    Absent: derived from rubyusbcmd (0->vendor, 1->ACM).
#   ruby_zlp=0|1      ACM echo ZLP; 0 = no ZLP (0301 default fix), 1 = 0300.
# The log channel keeps its per-512 frame ZLP rule regardless.
# ---
# 0300 = 0299 plus the pure-QMU TX cut-over (CL-0300):
#   - deletes the PIO TX path and every per-packet TX1CSR0 RMW
#     (TX_DMAREQEN toggles, TXPKTRDY kicks, deferred PIO Q_START);
#   - TX ownership is vendor mtu3_qmu.c: DMAREQEN once at prepare,
#     RESUME per enqueue, Q_START only with the first prepared GPD after
#     a prepare/stop/clear; the 0x18100 pseudo-active readback is no
#     longer consulted (start is software-state driven);
#   - CLEAR_FEATURE(HALT) 0x81/0x82 = vendor stall/toggle clear + standard
#     QMU queue restart (stop, flush ring, prepare);
#   - echo >512 B is split into <=512 B GPDs, ZLP only on the last chunk of
#     an exact 512-multiple transfer; non-ACM log path unchanged.
#   ruby_txreset=1     stall watchdog (FIFO-jam + silent-stop signatures)
#   ruby_txeprst=0     no EP_RST in the rebuild (ClearFeature owns toggle)
#   ruby_txreplay=0    0277 replay off (ring payloads are not resent)
#   ruby_cfgrst=0      no boot EP_RST (vendor parity)
#   ruby_clr01=1       CLEAR_FEATURE(0x01) RX light clear (0298)
#   ruby_rxbuf=512     RX GPD buflen (0299 default)
# Removed by 0300: ruby_txpio, ruby_txpiotail, ruby_qstart_ms,
# ruby_qstart_only, ruby_dmareq_pio, ruby_txkick, ruby_txrdy, ruby_txdeq,
# ruby_clr81, ruby_clrhalt, ruby_resume.
MACOS_VERSION=13.5
